Subject: sql: include <new> for std::nothrow
Last-Update: 2026-09-27

The file service's implementation allocates with new (std::nothrow) and
includes no header that declares std::nothrow; <new> does. Earlier libc++
releases brought <new> in through other standard headers; libc++ 23 does
not, and the file does not compile against it. It includes the header it
uses.

diff --git a/sql/server_component/mysql_file_imp.cc b/sql/server_component/mysql_file_imp.cc
index 346b38f..7b5b7ad 100644
--- a/sql/server_component/mysql_file_imp.cc
+++ b/sql/server_component/mysql_file_imp.cc
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ Foundation, Inc., 51 Franklin St, Fifth Floor, Boston, MA 02110-1301  USA */
 
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <mysql/components/service_implementation.h>
+#include <new>
 #include "my_io.h"
 #include "my_sys.h"
 
